    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a strong start. But some critics say that focusing on 'global duty' is actually a form of moral egoism—that we're just trying to feel good about ourselves while ignoring the urgent, systemic problems right here in our own backyard. How would you respond to the idea that it's actually *more* moral to prioritize the people in our own community first?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
